      "message": "This works when `g_lag_in_frames \u003d\u003d 0`, but crashes in `AOM_USAGE_GOOD_QUALITY` when `g_lag_in_frames` is left at its default (`lap_enabled \u003d\u003d 1`):\n- Before `ENCODE_STAGE` fails, `LAP_STAGE` has already pushed a `FIRSTPASS_STATS` entry (`stats_in_end++`) and `process_first_pass_stats()` has incremented `cpi-\u003etwopass_frame.stats_in++`.\n- Because `longjmp` skips `av1_twopass_postencode_update()` (`input_stats_lap()`) and `update_keyframe_counters()` (`av1_firstpass_info_move_cur_index*`), `stats_in_end` is not decremented; on the next `aom_codec_encode()` call, `cpi_lap` overflows `num_lap_buffers + 1` in `update_firstpass_stats()` (`firstpass.c:1018`) where `cpi_lap-\u003etwopass_frame.stats_in \u003d\u003d NULL`, causing a SEGV (reproducible in `EncodeAfterFailedFrameGoodQuality` by removing `cfg.g_lag_in_frames \u003d 0` and encoding 36 frames).",
