      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the review. The SEGV also happens without this change. On the parent 05acd5cd25, GQ with the default lag crashes in update_firstpass_stats() (firstpass.c:1024) on the call after the failed one in about half the runs, and in the other runs every later frame fails. The LAP stage pushes a stats entry on every call, the failed frame never uses its entry, and the overflow branch then reads cpi_lap-\u003etwopass_frame.stats_in, which is NULL.\n\nI tried also dropping the LAP stats entry and moving firstpass_info. The next frame then asserts in init_gop_frames_for_tpl(), because gf_frame_index, show_frame_count and frame_number would have to move too, and the GF group can still point at the dropped frame. A proper drop with lag is most of av1_post_encode_updates() for a frame that stopped half way. So PS3 drops the frame only in one pass mode with lag 0, where the lookahead holds just that frame. Other modes behave as before.",
